s=\"questionWidget-choicesTable\"><tbody><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-140497-a\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\" style=\"background: rgb(64, 64, 64); color: white;\">a</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-140497-b\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">b</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">II only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-140497-c\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">c</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I and II only</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-140497-d\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">d</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">None of the statements are true</td></tr><tr><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetter\"><div id=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-140497-e\" class=\"questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle\">e</div></td><td class=\"questionWidget-choiceText\">I and III only</td></tr></tbody></table><div class=\"questionWidget-buttonBar\"><div class=\"questionWidget-submitButton disabledButton\" style=\"display: none;\">Submit</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-spinnerFrame\"><div class=\"questionWidget-spinner\" style=\"display: block;\"></div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-result\"><div class=\"questionWidget-incorrectIcon\"><img src=\"/img/incorrect-answer.svg\"></div><div class=\"questionWidget-incorrectText\">Incorrect</div></div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanationHeader\">EXPLANATION</div><div class=\"questionWidget-explanation\"><p>Recall that a set of vectors in an inner product space is orthogonal if all vectors in the set are mutually orthogonal with respect to the given inner product. </p>\n<p>With that in mind, let's examine our statements in tur